{
  "id": "spxx677",
  "title": "CHAPTER 6 : PROFIT AND LOSS – ZERO GAP AUTHOR EDITION",
  "order": 8,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "1vwrvg0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Introduction to Profit and Loss"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Core Chapter",
          "value": "Chapter 6",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Exam Focus",
          "value": "RRB & Competitive Exams",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Key Model",
          "value": "False Weights",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Important Trick",
          "value": "Equal Profit & Loss",
          "icon": "check"
        }
      ],
      "id": "t7imik1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z9mkhv7",
      "content": "Profit and Loss is one of the most scoring chapters in RRB mathematics. It is based on simple commercial transactions — buying and selling."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "516gefk",
      "content": "Key Terms:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a4272yw",
      "content": "Cost Price (CP): The price at which an article is purchased. Selling Price (SP): The price at which the article is sold."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9sddwc5",
      "content": "If SP &gt; CP → Profit If CP &gt; SP → Loss"
    },
    {
      "id": "zhfwvdw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Basic Formulas"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pzmwg31",
      "content": "Profit = SP − CP Loss = CP − SP"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5zhjgww",
      "content": "Profit % = (Profit / CP) × 100 Loss % = (Loss / CP) × 100 Important:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8e4g5lc",
      "content": "Profit or loss percentage is ALWAYS calculated on Cost Price unless stated otherwise."
    },
    {
      "id": "jkonktd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Finding Profit"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dakobxv",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kkwp9gt",
      "content": "A shopkeeper buys a pen for ₹40 and sells it for ₹55. Find the profit and profit percentage. Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uqhhecy",
      "content": "Step 1: Find profit. Profit = 55 − 40 = ₹15"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j9p7zd2",
      "content": "Step 2: Calculate profit percentage. Profit % = (15/40) × 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "om38fzl",
      "content": "= 37.5%"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ncwa294",
      "content": "Final Answer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iixwlgj",
      "content": "Profit = ₹15, Profit % = 37.5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "n2gwtm1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Finding Loss"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8bzipz9",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sj96fna",
      "content": "A trader buys a book for ₹120 and sells it for ₹96. Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jzac3og",
      "content": "Step 1: Find loss. Loss = 120 − 96 = ₹24"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fcdbg41",
      "content": "Step 2: Loss percentage. Loss % = (24/120) × 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "dr4x22f",
      "content": "= 20%"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "47014vo",
      "content": "Final Answer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ftoebnt",
      "content": "Loss = ₹24, Loss % = 20%"
    },
    {
      "id": "3guu75h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Finding Selling Price"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1v01tel",
      "content": "Formula: SP = CP × (100 + Profit%) / 100 Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ms8f3ow",
      "content": "Find SP if CP = ₹500 and profit = 20%."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "aet7g8z",
      "content": "=&gt;SP = 500 × (120/100)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2sjys38",
      "content": "= 600"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d8yw074",
      "content": "Final Answer: Selling Price = ₹600."
    },
    {
      "id": "1gpg3ka",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Finding Cost Price"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "edrev61",
      "content": "Formula: CP = SP × 100 / (100 + Profit%)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tw2oh0r",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jfphtsx",
      "content": "An article is sold for ₹780 at a profit of 30%. Find CP."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2qqtecj",
      "content": "=&gt; CP = 780 × 100 / 130"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "bn57u26",
      "content": "= 600"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vre698f",
      "content": "Final Answer: Cost Price = ₹600."
    },
    {
      "id": "28kwqgf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Loss-Based Selling Price"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ni2qe1s",
      "content": "Formula: SP = CP × (100 − Loss%) / 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "skzfdff",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r565w73",
      "content": "CP = ₹900, Loss = 10%. SP = 900 × 90/100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "g9t6lac",
      "content": "= 810"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jgnallq",
      "content": "Final Answer: ₹810."
    },
    {
      "id": "mimuzy2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Discount and Marked Price"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3pu1v8k",
      "content": "Marked Price (MP): The labeled price on an article. Discount: Reduction offered on MP."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c7noufr",
      "content": "SP = MP − Discount Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rbvuvty",
      "content": "MP = ₹1000, Discount = 20%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tf6boje",
      "content": "=&gt;Discount amount = 200 SP = 800"
    },
    {
      "id": "k793yvq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Successive Discounts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ymvdx46",
      "content": "Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3x1ln8h",
      "content": "Net Discount = a + b − (ab/100)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j11f83s",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nrovtvo",
      "content": "Discounts of 20% and 10%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zl47erb",
      "content": "=&gt;Net = 20 + 10 − 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "cawp7pv",
      "content": "= 28%"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pczfrbb",
      "content": "Important:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ikhu1ex",
      "content": "Discounts are not added directly."
    },
    {
      "id": "vnc3yp7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Markup and Profit Relationship"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kebdczv",
      "content": "Sometimes sellers increase MP to ensure profit even after discount."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ruc2hfc",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "843j94n",
      "content": "A shopkeeper marks goods 40% above CP and gives a discount of 20%. Find profit. Solution: Assume CP = 100."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "09xcwp3",
      "content": "MP = 140"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qj95fc5",
      "content": "Discount = 20% of 140 = 28"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "h1qansb",
      "content": "SP = 112"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mij69a7",
      "content": "Profit = 12%."
    },
    {
      "id": "3ie1we5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Dishonest Shopkeeper – False Weights"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Markup with Discount (Very Important RRB Model)",
      "id": "recnzyq"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vqnkpy9",
      "content": "When a shopkeeper uses less weight but charges full price, extra profit occurs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cgq3u9p",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b3g52u0",
      "content": "A trader claims to sell 1 kg but actually sells 900 g. Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e5rvn3g",
      "content": "Profit % = (100/90 − 1) × 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gt75ic9",
      "content": "≈ 11.11%"
    },
    {
      "id": "w9gu551",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Profit When Selling Two Articles Together"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rd7orzn",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cx2xx4k",
      "content": "One article sold at 20% profit and another at 20% loss. Find net result. Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6o2k9ei",
      "content": "Assume CP of both = 100. SP1 = 120"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lte4tfx",
      "content": "SP2 = 80"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yb86bl7",
      "content": "Total CP = 200 Total SP = 200"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "an6ckrg",
      "content": "Net Result: No profit, no loss."
    },
    {
      "id": "iryqxbv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Equal Profit and Loss Trick (Important)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nvaqqpc",
      "content": "If two items are sold at equal % profit and loss, there is always a NET LOSS. Formula: Loss % = (x²)/100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "laoam7a",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hllbzrd",
      "content": "20% profit and 20% loss. Solution: Loss = 400/100 = 4%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s386kpv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Profit Based on Selling Price"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f50un1e",
      "content": "Sometimes profit is given as percentage of SP."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7b5usp9",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5c66suh",
      "content": "Profit is 20% of SP. Find profit % on CP. Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "se5ypbq",
      "content": "Let SP = 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mecqk6a",
      "content": "Profit = 20"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zdkor78",
      "content": "CP = 80"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "796n8yv",
      "content": "Profit % on CP = (20/80)×100 = 25%"
    },
    {
      "id": "ni5rcce",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Advanced Concept — Successive Profit </strong>Example: Increase price by 10% and then 20%. Solution: Net change = 10 + 20 + 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8mos9wb",
      "content": "= 32% increase."
    },
    {
      "id": "tocpp6l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Solved Examples IMPORTANT FORMULAS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w2ftvvi",
      "content": "Cost Price (CP): Price at which an article is bought. Selling Price (SP): Price at which an article is sold. Profit = SP − CP"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "omqwpau",
      "content": "Loss = CP − SP"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rqzjyjz",
      "content": "Profit % = (Profit / CP) × 100 Loss % = (Loss / CP) × 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "37rdb2f",
      "content": "SP = CP × (100 + Profit%) / 100 SP = CP × (100 − Loss%) / 100 CP = SP × 100 / (100 + Profit%) CP = SP × 100 / (100 − Loss%)"
    },
    {
      "id": "ftyj941",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SMART EXAM TRICKS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Profit and Loss calculations are primarily evaluated relative to the Cost Price (CP) unless specifically calculated on Selling Price (SP).",
        "Discounts are always offered on the Marked Price (MP) to determine the final Selling Price (SP).",
        "Successive discounts require step-by-step reduction or the application of the effective discount percentage formula.",
        "Dishonest shopkeeper problems determine profit percentage based on the true weight versus the false weight used.",
        "Equal profit and loss scenarios on two articles sold at the same selling price result in an overall loss percentage."
      ],
      "id": "3aboqka"
    },
    {
      "id": "rfddlja",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Profit and loss percentages are ALWAYS calculated on Cost Price unless stated otherwise.",
        "Successive Discount Trick: Net Discount = a + b − (ab/100)",
        "Equal Profit and Loss Trick: If two items are sold at x% profit and x% loss → Net Loss = x² / 100",
        "False Weight Trick: Profit % = (Error / True Weight) × 100",
        "Markup Strategy: If goods are marked up and then discounted, ALWAYS assume CP = 100 for faster calculations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Concept",
        "Base Parameter",
        "Condition / Formula"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Profit",
          "Cost Price (CP)",
          "SP > CP (Profit = SP - CP)"
        ],
        [
          "Loss",
          "Cost Price (CP)",
          "CP > SP (Loss = CP - SP)"
        ],
        [
          "Discount",
          "Marked Price (MP)",
          "MP > SP (Discount = MP - SP)"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "n8eiokk"
    },
    {
      "id": "oesl6jl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SOLVED EXAMPLES"
    },
    {
      "id": "90qwxgf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 1: Find Profit and Profit Percentage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iwufam6",
      "content": "A shopkeeper buys a watch for ₹800 and sells it for ₹1000."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ewqoi5p",
      "content": "Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qnrkzc0",
      "content": "Step 1: Calculate Profit. Profit = 1000 − 800 = ₹200"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gruu779",
      "content": "Step 2: Calculate Profit %. Profit % = (200 / 800) × 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9rtvzqa",
      "content": "= 25%"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m7rwshw",
      "content": "Final Answer: Profit = ₹200, Profit % = 25%."
    },
    {
      "id": "yj1vn1a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 2: Find Selling Price"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fopp9iy",
      "content": "Find the selling price of an article with CP = ₹500 and profit = 20%. Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b2orqmw",
      "content": "Step 1: Use formula. SP = CP × (120/100)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7gc8nm9",
      "content": "Step 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g3urzx0",
      "content": "SP = 500 × 1.2 = ₹600"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pflrr77",
      "content": "Final Answer: Selling Price = ₹600."
    },
    {
      "id": "lgazkon",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 3: Marked Price and Discount"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oul5d6y",
      "content": "A shirt is marked at ₹1500. A discount of 10% is offered. Find SP. Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xthi03v",
      "content": "Step 1: Find discount. 10% of 1500 = ₹150"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9hh55ca",
      "content": "Step 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1ktoltb",
      "content": "SP = 1500 − 150 = ₹1350"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r3807ti",
      "content": "Final Answer: Selling Price = ₹1350."
    },
    {
      "id": "6ticnyc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 4: Markup with Discount (Very Important RRB Model)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qrf247z",
      "content": "A shopkeeper marks goods 25% above CP and gives a discount of 10%. Find profit %. Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l28tdbf",
      "content": "Step 1: Assume CP = 100."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fow96ea",
      "content": "Step 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "yh5w98b",
      "content": "MP = 125"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2x5ptp4",
      "content": "Step 3:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8q637dh",
      "content": "Discount = 10% of 125 = 12.5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9yupmou",
      "content": "Step 4:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gnqxvp9",
      "content": "SP = 125 − 12.5 = 112.5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j40f89n",
      "content": "Step 5:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1tm5pk7",
      "content": "Profit = 112.5 − 100 = 12.5"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nlo07td",
      "content": "Profit % = 12.5%"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qr7z6nu",
      "content": "Final Answer: Profit = 12.5%."
    },
    {
      "id": "x9yt3dj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 5: False Weight"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "359jtej",
      "content": "A trader sells 900 g sugar as 1 kg. Find profit %. Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5bwuaq2",
      "content": "Step 1:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qh4ex2u",
      "content": "True weight = 1000 g Error = 100 g"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1gz4r2f",
      "content": "Step 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2subxmf",
      "content": "Profit % = (100 / 900) × 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "blomedb",
      "content": "≈ 11.11%"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8n3uun1",
      "content": "Final Answer: Profit ≈ 11.11%."
    },
    {
      "id": "r46gxpl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Practice Questions with Detailed Solutions"
    },
    {
      "id": "jh27f3t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Markup with Discount is a high-yield model frequently tested in RRB and national competitive examinations.",
        "Pay attention to examiner traps where profit percentage is calculated on Selling Price rather than Cost Price.",
        "False weight problems require careful identification of actual quantity delivered versus claimed weight."
      ],
      "id": "ldbcx1l"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8goq288",
      "content": "Find the loss % if CP = ₹750 and SP = ₹675. Loss = 75"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v05qlrw",
      "content": "Loss % = (75/750) × 100 = 10%."
    },
    {
